---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="GeoScore v1.9: Live GEO Score SVG Badges & Stack Guides | GeoScore"
  description="GeoScore v1.9 launches live SVG score badges for READMEs, automatic Shopify/WordPress/Next.js detection in Chrome MV3, 6 platform playbooks, and 3-mode web audits."
  schema={[
    {
      '@type': 'Article',
      headline: 'GeoScore v1.9: Live GEO Score SVG Badges, Stack Auto-Detection & Platform Playbooks',
      description: 'GeoScore v1.9 launches live SVG score badges for GitHub READMEs and footers, automatic Shopify/WordPress/Next.js stack detection in Chrome Extension v1.9.0, 6 new platform guides, and unified 3-mode web audits.',
      url: 'https://geoscore.help/blog/geoscore-v1-9-live-badges-stack-detection/',
      datePublished: '2026-11-25',
      dateModified: '2026-11-25',
      author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'GeoScore' },
      publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'GeoScore', url: 'https://geoscore.help' }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'FAQPage',
      mainEntity: [
        {
          '@type': 'Question',
          name: 'How do GeoScore live SVG badges work?',
          acceptedAnswer: {
            '@type': 'Answer',
            text: 'Point any Markdown or HTML image tag at https://geoscore.help/badge/yourdomain.com. A Cloudflare Pages edge function audits your public site, caches the SVG badge for 6 hours, and color-codes your 0-100 score across four tiers (86+ emerald, 68+ blue, 36+ amber, under 36 red).'
          }
        },
        {
          '@type': 'Question',
          name: 'Which tech stacks does GeoScore Chrome Extension v1.9.0 detect automatically?',
          acceptedAnswer: {
            '@type': 'Answer',
            text: 'GeoScore Chrome Extension v1.9.0 automatically detects Shopify, WordPress, and Next.js on the active tab and displays stack-specific deployment steps for llms.txt, robots.txt, and JSON-LD schema directly inside the Side Panel.'
          }
        },
        {
          '@type': 'Question',
          name: 'Does the live badge endpoint expose private or internal IP addresses?',
          acceptedAnswer: {
            '@type': 'Answer',
            text: 'No. The /badge/[domain] edge function enforces strict domain validation, SSRF and private-IP blocking, manual redirect checks, and a 350 KB streaming read cap so only public production domains are scored.'
          }
        },
        {
          '@type': 'Question',
          name: 'How accurate is the background tab score badge in Chrome Extension v1.9.0?',
          acceptedAnswer: {
            '@type': 'Answer',
            text: 'Version 1.9.0 upgrades the background service worker to inspect all six non-HTML discovery endpoints (robots.txt, llms.txt, sitemap.xml, /ai/summary.json, /ai/faq.json, and /.well-known/ai-plugin.json) alongside the active page so toolbar scores match full Side Panel audits.'
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]}
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-8">
    <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
      <div class="text-center mb-10">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-geo-500/10 text-geo-400 border border-geo-500/20 mb-4">
          Release v1.9.0 · Extension, Badges &amp; Platform Playbooks
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold mb-3 text-white leading-tight">
          GeoScore v1.9: Live GEO Score SVG Badges, Stack Auto-Detection &amp; Platform Playbooks
        </h1>
        <p class="text-gray-400">Published November 25, 2026 · 6 min read</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6 border border-brand-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-950/20 to-geo-950/30">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-1">Live Now on Web &amp; Chrome Web Store (v1.9.0)</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-300">Dynamic SVG score badges, automatic Shopify/WordPress/Next.js detection, 6-endpoint background scoring, and unified 3-mode web audits.</p>
          </div>
          <a
            href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/geoscore-free-geo-aeo-llm/cboppgehhkhaamcgfcikhekkdaelichn"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-semibold text-white bg-gradient-to-r from-geo-600 to-brand-600 hover:from-geo-500 hover:to-brand-500 transition shadow-lg shadow-geo-600/20 shrink-0 text-sm"
          >
            Install Extension v1.9.0 →
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-base leading-relaxed">
          Finding GEO issues is only half the workflow. Developers and site owners kept asking for two things: a lightweight way to showcase verified AI readiness in GitHub READMEs and site footers, and concrete deployment instructions tailored to their exact CMS or framework instead of generic server advice.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">
          <strong class="text-white">GeoScore v1.9.0</strong> ships both across <a href="/" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">geoscore.help</a> and the official <a href="/blog/geoscore-chrome-extension-launch/" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Chrome MV3 Extension</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">1. Live Dynamic GEO Score SVG Badges (Embed in 10 Seconds)</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Every public domain now has a live, cache-backed SVG badge at <code class="text-geo-400">https://geoscore.help/badge/&lt;domain&gt;</code>. Powered by a Cloudflare Pages edge function with SSRF/private-IP filtering, manual redirect verification, a 350 KB streaming read cap, and a 6-hour edge cache, the badge automatically reflects your latest 0–100 score and color tier (<strong class="text-emerald-400">86+ green</strong>, <strong class="text-brand-400">68+ blue</strong>, <strong class="text-yellow-400">36+ amber</strong>, <strong class="text-red-400">&lt;36 red</strong>).
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/70 border border-gray-800 mb-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
          <div class="text-xs text-gray-400">Live example rendered directly from the edge endpoint:</div>
          <a href="/?url=https://geoscore.help" class="shrink-0">
            <img src="/badge/geoscore.help" alt="GeoScore live GEO readiness badge" class="h-6" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-brand-400 mb-2">Markdown Snippet (GitHub README / Docs)</h3>
        <div class="bg-gray-900/80 rounded-xl p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-300 mb-4 overflow-x-auto border border-gray-800">
<pre>{`[![GEO Score](https://geoscore.help/badge/example.com)](https://geoscore.help/?url=https://example.com)`}</pre>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-brand-400 mb-2">HTML Snippet (Website Footer / Status Page)</h3>
        <div class="bg-gray-900/80 rounded-xl p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-300 mb-4 overflow-x-auto border border-gray-800">
<pre>{`<a href="https://geoscore.help/?url=https://example.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
  <img src="https://geoscore.help/badge/example.com" alt="GEO Score" />
</a>`}</pre>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">
          In <strong class="text-white">Chrome Extension v1.9.0</strong>, the Side Panel renders a live badge preview automatically after every audit with one-click Markdown and HTML copy buttons—no manual domain typing needed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">2. Automatic Stack Detection &amp; Dedicated Platform Playbooks</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Deploying <code class="text-geo-400">/llms.txt</code>, <code class="text-geo-400">robots.txt</code> AI crawler rules, and JSON-LD schema looks completely different on Shopify vs WordPress vs Next.js App Router. GeoScore v1.9.0 introduces automatic stack detection inside the Chrome extension (<code class="text-geo-400">stackDetector.js</code>) and a 4-tab deployment guide (<strong class="text-white">Static HTML</strong>, <strong class="text-white">Next.js</strong>, <strong class="text-white">WordPress</strong>, <strong class="text-white">Shopify</strong>) right inside the web Fix Files panel.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4">
          <a href="/geo-for/shopify/" class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800 hover:border-geo-500/50 transition block">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono text-geo-400 mb-1">/geo-for/shopify/</div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-base mb-1">GEO for Shopify</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Upload <code class="text-gray-300">llms.txt</code> via Content &gt; Files + URL redirect, customize <code class="text-gray-300">robots.txt.liquid</code>, and complete Product JSON-LD.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/geo-for/wordpress/" class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800 hover:border-geo-500/50 transition block">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono text-geo-400 mb-1">/geo-for/wordpress/</div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-base mb-1">GEO for WordPress</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Place root <code class="text-gray-300">llms.txt</code>, configure Yoast / Rank Math AI crawler rules, and inject schema cleanly via WPCode.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/geo-for/nextjs/" class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800 hover:border-geo-500/50 transition block">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono text-geo-400 mb-1">/geo-for/nextjs/</div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-base mb-1">GEO for Next.js</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Ship <code class="text-gray-300">public/llms.txt</code>, typed <code class="text-gray-300">app/robots.ts</code>, Server Component JSON-LD, and localhost SSR vs CSR checks.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">
          Prefer hands-free implementation? When an audit scores below 60, GeoScore now surfaces the one-time <a href="/fixpack/" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline font-medium">$49 Fix Pack</a> (custom llms.txt, robots.txt, schema, and post-deploy re-audit within 48 hours). Reach us anytime at <a href="mailto:hello@geoscore.help" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">hello@geoscore.help</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">3. Accurate 6-Endpoint Background Scoring &amp; 3-Mode Web Audits</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-300">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-geo-400 mb-1">Full 6-Endpoint Silent Background Audit (Extension v1.9.0)</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
              Previously, silent toolbar badge checks only sampled a subset of discovery files, which could under-report scores compared to opening the Side Panel. In v1.9.0, the MV3 service worker checks all six non-HTML discovery endpoints—<code class="text-gray-300">robots.txt</code>, <code class="text-gray-300">llms.txt</code>, <code class="text-gray-300">sitemap.xml</code>, <code class="text-gray-300">/ai/summary.json</code>, <code class="text-gray-300">/ai/faq.json</code>, and <code class="text-gray-300">/.well-known/ai-plugin.json</code>—so your toolbar badge score matches the full Side Panel report.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-brand-400 mb-1">Unified 3-Tab Hero Switcher on geoscore.help</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
              On the web app, you can now switch cleanly between <strong class="text-white">Single URL</strong>, <strong class="text-white">Batch Sitemap</strong>, and <strong class="text-white">Compare Sites</strong> directly inside the hero audit panel—making competitor benchmarking and multi-page audits much faster.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">How do GeoScore live SVG badges work?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400">Point any Markdown or HTML image tag at <code class="text-geo-400">https://geoscore.help/badge/yourdomain.com</code>. A Cloudflare Pages edge function audits your public site, caches the SVG badge for 6 hours, and color-codes your 0–100 score across four tiers (86+ emerald, 68+ blue, 36+ amber, under 36 red).</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">Which tech stacks does GeoScore Chrome Extension v1.9.0 detect automatically?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400">GeoScore Chrome Extension v1.9.0 automatically detects <a href="/geo-for/shopify/" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Shopify</a>, <a href="/geo-for/wordpress/" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">WordPress</a>, and <a href="/geo-for/nextjs/" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Next.js</a> locally inside your browser and displays stack-specific deployment steps directly inside the Side Panel.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">Does the live badge endpoint expose private or internal IP addresses?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400">No. The <code class="text-geo-400">/badge/[domain]</code> edge function enforces strict domain validation, SSRF and private-IP blocking, manual redirect checks, and a 350 KB streaming read cap so only public production domains are scored.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">How accurate is the background tab score badge in Chrome Extension v1.9.0?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400">Version 1.9.0 upgrades the background service worker to inspect all six non-HTML discovery endpoints (<code class="text-geo-400">robots.txt</code>, <code class="text-geo-400">llms.txt</code>, <code class="text-geo-400">sitemap.xml</code>, <code class="text-geo-400">/ai/summary.json</code>, <code class="text-geo-400">/ai/faq.json</code>, and <code class="text-geo-400">/.well-known/ai-plugin.json</code>) so toolbar scores match full Side Panel audits.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6 bg-gradient-to-r from-geo-500/10 to-brand-500/10 border border-brand-500/30">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">Try GeoScore v1.9.0 &amp; Embed Your Live Badge</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-5 leading-relaxed">
          Audit your site across 11 GEO dimensions, copy your live SVG score badge, and deploy stack-ready fix files in minutes.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <a
            href="/"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-semibold text-white bg-gradient-to-r from-geo-600 to-brand-600 hover:from-geo-500 hover:to-brand-500 transition shadow-lg shadow-geo-600/20"
          >
            Run Free Web Audit →
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/geoscore-free-geo-aeo-llm/cboppgehhkhaamcgfcikhekkdaelichn"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-semibold text-gray-200 bg-gray-800/80 hover:bg-gray-700/80 hover:text-white transition border border-gray-700"
          >
            Chrome Extension v1.9.0
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
